A||||4||Jncomutt||GT Exhaust Tips.. Which side???||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||12-03-2001||08:45 PM||||OK, I picked up a used set of GT exhaust (megaphone style) tips.   I'm taking them to the shop to get them mounted with my new cat/muffler/piping.  The problem is, I don't know which side is which.  I thought they were the same at first, but when you look at them closely, you notice that one has about a 2" straight piece just before the Y split, whereas the other one goes basically right into the curve.  So... which is which??||||reg||1
Z||000001||RossT||12-03-2001||11:10 PM||||If you have an 88 the L and R are the same part# and they have the same bend and length.<P>If you have a pre-88, set the tips with the megaphone end on the ground next to each other.  The one that is longer is the left side and the shorter one is the right side.<BR>The will only install one way.  If you do it wrong one side will stick out an inch or two more than the other.<P>Recently I purchased a set of stock tips for my 88 fromula and found that you can not use the 85-87 ones.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever3000||12-03-2001||11:27 PM||||Hang on there, Ross.  I'm not where I can look at my 88GT right now, but last time I was underneath it I noticed my RH tips had the longer pipe before the Y.  I'm 99% sure.  Will check later tonight.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||12-03-2001||11:48 PM||||Yes Ross I also think it's the left side that is longer?<BR>The tip on top is the right side (Short):<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=13270947&p=51150513&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P>Not a very good shot.....but look close:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=13270947&p=50378527&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P>DXR_DAD<P>||||reg||5
Z||000004||Jncomutt||12-04-2001||10:57 AM||||Thank You guys, that was exactly the info I was looking for.  Knew you could help me out...||||reg||1
